  "body": "From M5's review of PR #1634 (#1631), non-blocking there. After #1634, a 2D Chamfer whose source is a stock flush with the part's footprint is refused on the op by the solid law (the break would be a V-groove into the part). That refusal reads as a generic `Gouge`; it does not say the workaround - choose the part as the chamfer's source, which gives the same path. MCP `add_operation` defaults to the stock source, so agents hit it with no hint.\n\nDone means: the refusal on a stock-source chamfer that breaks into a part names the cause and the workaround (\"chamfer with the part as source\"); pinned over MCP and generate.",
